  "youtube": {
    "title": "Why \"Calm Down\" Never Works #shorts",
    "description": "Telling yourself to calm down usually makes it worse. Try this instead: name the feeling. \"I feel anxious.\" \"I'm angry.\"\n\nIn a UCLA brain-scan study, people who put a word to an emotional image showed less activity in the amygdala, the brain's alarm system, than people who didn't. Psychologists call it affect labeling.\n\nNext time it hits: pause, and say (or write) exactly what you feel. One word is enough.\n\nResearch: Lieberman et al. (2007), \"Putting Feelings Into Words\", Psychological Science.\n\n#shorts #anxiety #psychology #emotions #mentalhealth #animation #selfimprovement",
